---
source: crates/oxc_formatter_css/tests/fixtures/mod.rs
---
==================== Input ====================
// A sign glued to a function-call operand inside a calculation is a folded
// binary operator (same subtraction as the value-position path, see
// value-glued-minus.scss), parsed as a `Calc` operation whose printer keeps
// the source glue verbatim — matching Prettier byte-for-byte here.
// dart-sass itself rejects the glued form inside calculations
// ("+" and "-" must be surrounded by whitespace), so no valid input changes.
// A SPACED `-1` stays a signed value (`x -1` is two list elements, not
// subtraction), and word-glued runs (`100%-20px`) stay one verbatim word.
.a {
  width: max(map-get($m, a)-1, 0);
  height: min(map-get($m, a) -1, 0);
  margin: max(100%-20px, 0px);
  // the split-off dimension keeps its multiplicative tail (`- (1px * 2)`)
  padding: max(map-get($m, a)-1px * 2, 0px);
}

